# Extracted game assets NEVER enter git.
#
# This repo is intended to become public. Git history cannot be un-published:
# once Embark's meshes, textures and item icons land in a commit they are
# permanent even after a later delete, and a private repo that goes public
# publishes its whole history at once. Only the curated layer is publishable —
# the application code, and the catalog metadata in src/data/items.json.
#
# Everything below is produced locally by the extraction and bake pipeline and
# is expected to be missing on a fresh clone. See README "Assets" and CREDITS.
/public/items/
/public/models/
/scripts/generated/
/visual-diff/
/_objcheck/

# Note: an earlier rule here kept /public/models/body/ tracked while the rest
# was hosted off-repo (scripts/publish-models.mjs + VITE_MODELS_BASE). The base
# body meshes are Embark's too, so that exception is gone. The off-repo hosting
# path still works and is the only route to a deployed site that renders.

# Staged copy of exactly what the asset host must serve, built from public/ by
# scripts/stage-assets.mjs. Same extracted artwork, so the same rule applies.
/_assets-upload/

# Ad-hoc render probes dropped at the root by the audit/debug scripts. Renders of
# extracted geometry are extracted material.
/probe_*.png

# Local Netlify link folder
.netlify

# Private archive configuration (may contain server/channel metadata)
/scripts/discord-export/channels.local.json

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

.DS_Store
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.env
.env.local

*.log
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated by scripts/import-catalog.ts
scripts/import-report.txt

# generated by scripts/bake-all.mjs
scripts/bake-all.report.json

# Generated verdict store — regenerable by npm run verify, and its presence
# changes test results, so it must never be tracked or relied on by tests.
/scripts/verification.generated.json

# Reasonix session/state directory.
/.reasonix/
